{"uid":"thag2.17","title":"Tissa (3rd)","reference":"Theragāthā 2.17","blocks":[{"kind":"verse","lines":["A shaven one wrapped in the outer robe","gets many enemies","when they receive food and drink,","clothes and bedding.","Knowing this danger,","this great fear in honors,","a mendicant should wander mindful,","with few possessions, not festering."]}]}
